          "id": "N4",
          "good": false,
          "decisions": [
            {
              "about": "Two key results",
              "decided": "one how well the people use each deliverable, and one how long the user waits for it. Asking only the user's points shows in the second",
              "by": "user"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "N5",
          "good": true,
          "decisions": []
        },
        {
          "id": "N6",
          "good": false,
          "decisions": [
            {
              "about": "The concept",
              "decided": "rn moves the work toward the goal by the vital few and piles up none of the trivial many. It draws out what the user really wants along the design tree, plans, makes, and asks by best practice, judges and improves each deliverable by its people, goes back to the tree on a problem, and revises the tree on each run by what the run found",
              "by": "user"
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "rn's design says how a turn carries out a best practice",
      "path": "dev/rn/architecture.md",
      "kind": "architecture",
      "inputs": [
        "dev/rn/product-vision.md"
      ],
      "preconditions": [],
      "status": "doing",
      "necessary_conditions": [
        {
          "id": "N1",
          "good": false,
          "decisions": []
        },
        {
          "id": "N2",
          "good": false,
          "decisions": []
        },
        {
          "id": "N3",
          "good": false,
          "decisions": []
        },
        {
          "id": "N4",
          "good": false,
          "decisions": [
            {
              "about": "A turn",
              "decided": "once the main conversation settles a deliverable's decisions, a turn makes it from them and its kind's best practice until every intent is good, or a point only the user can settle stops it",
              "by": "user"
            },
            {
              "about": "Good from the root",
              "decided": "a shortfall goes back to the decision that serves it, and the next round makes the deliverable from the design, never a fix beside it",
              "by": "user"
            },
            {
              "about": "A remark during a turn",
              "decided": "a remark during a turn is a point: the main conversation settles it into the tree, and the turn goes on from the changed design. No one adds it to a running role",
              "by": "user"
            },
            {
              "about": "The maker checks first",
              "decided": "the generator reads the deliverable as its people before it hands it on. Only the evaluators make an intent good",
              "by": "reasoning"
            },
            {
              "about": "The evaluator seeks the good",
              "decided": "an evaluator reads as the deliverable's people and confirms where each intent gives them what they're after. For an intent not yet good, it says what would make it good, and it looks for no fault beyond that",
              "by": "user"
            },
            {
              "about": "The designer judges the evaluators",
              "decided": "the main conversation judges what each evaluator says would make an intent good by the design tree and the purpose. Only what the people need and what asks for intent goes on, back to the decision that serves it, never onto the deliverable",
              "by": "user"
            },
            {
              "about": "Intent in the tree",
              "decided": "a design tree holds what each deliverable is for and the decisions that serve it. The generator settles how a deliverable works inside as it makes it",
              "by": "user"
            },
            {
              "about": "Lessons before the merge",
              "decided": "before the user merges, rn proposes each change to a best practice that the run's points and lacks call for, and each change the user takes becomes a deliverable of the run",
              "by": "user"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
